---
// Crest privacy policy. Moved here from adrieltte.github.io/crest-privacy so
// the Google OAuth consent screen's home page and privacy policy share one
// verified domain. Keep it in step with what the app actually does.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Crest Privacy Policy: Applied Theory"
  description="What data the Crest gym tracker for Android handles, where it is stored, and how to delete it."
>
  <div class="container policy">
    <h1 class="display">Crest Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective 3 October 2026 · Developer: Applied Theory</p>
    <Prose>
      <p>
        Crest is a gym workout tracker for Android. This policy explains what data the app handles,
        where it is stored, and how you can delete it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>In short: your workouts stay on your phone.</strong> The developer runs no servers and
        never receives your data. If you turn on Google Drive backup, copies go to your own Google
        Drive, which only you and the app can access.
      </p>

      <h2>Data the app stores</h2>
      <p>Crest stores the following only on your device, in the app's private storage:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your workouts: exercises, sets, weights, reps, notes, and start and finish times.</li>
        <li>Your workout templates and custom exercises.</li>
        <li>Your settings, such as weight unit, bar weight, plates and rest time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Crest has no account system, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. It does not
        collect your location, contacts, photos or any identifier for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Backups you choose to make</h2>
      <p>Crest sends data off your phone only when you choose one of these:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Drive backup.</strong> If you connect Google Drive, Crest saves a copy of
          your data after each finished workout and keeps the 10 newest copies. Copies are stored in
          Crest's hidden app folder in your own Google Drive. Crest asks only for the
          <code>drive.appdata</code> permission, which gives it access to that folder and nothing
          else in your Drive. The app also reads your Google account email address, only to show you
          which account it backs up to. This data goes directly from your phone to Google. The
          developer never receives it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Device folder backup.</strong> If you choose a folder, Crest saves the same copies
          into that folder on your device. If that folder is synced by another app, that app's
          privacy policy applies to the copies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Manual export.</strong> When you tap Export, Crest creates a file and opens the
          Android share menu. The file goes wherever you choose to send it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Android may also include the app's data in your device's own backup to your Google account,
        depending on your phone's backup settings. Google manages that backup, not Crest.
      </p>

      <h2>Google user data</h2>
      <p>
        Crest's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will
        adhere to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements. Crest uses Google Drive access only to save and
        restore your own backups. It does not sell this data, use it for advertising, or let anyone
        else read it.
      </p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> to alert you when your rest between sets is over, and to show the workout in progress.</li>
        <li><strong>Alarms &amp; reminders (exact alarms):</strong> so the rest alert arrives on time. If you deny it, the alert still arrives, possibly a little late.</li>
        <li><strong>Vibration:</strong> for the rest alert.</li>
        <li><strong>Run at startup:</strong> to restore a pending rest alert after your phone restarts.</li>
        <li><strong>Internet:</strong> only for Google Drive backup.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To delete everything on your phone, uninstall Crest.</li>
        <li>To stop new backups, open Settings in Crest and tap Stop auto-backup.</li>
        <li>
          To delete the backups in Google Drive, open Google Drive on the web, go to Settings, then
          Manage apps, find Crest, and choose Delete hidden app data.
        </li>
        <li>
          To remove Crest's access to your Google account, visit
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          To delete copies in a device folder, delete the <code>crest-auto-*.json</code> files (and
          any <code>barlog-auto-*.json</code> from before the app was renamed) in that folder.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Crest is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:adrieltangte@gmail.com">adrieltangte@gmail.com</a></p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding-block: var(--space-9) 0;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    line-height: 0.95;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }
  .meta {
    margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    color: var(--c-ink-2);
  }
</style>
